## FFmpeg and ffprobe

Builds of Grape that include audio and video conversion ship FFmpeg, which converts the audio and video, and ffprobe, which reads media details. They aren't compiled into Grape: they're separate programs next to it, and Grape starts them when it needs them. Grape builds them itself from FFmpeg 9.0.2 with only the parts it uses, and without any networking code. They're under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later (GPL-2.0-or-later), because they include x264.

Those builds carry their license texts in a `licenses/ffmpeg` folder next to Grape: in Grape's install folder on Windows, and in `Grape.app/Contents/Resources/licenses/ffmpeg/` on macOS. `SOURCE.md` there gives the exact versions, the configure line, and where to get the complete source: `grape-ffmpeg-sources.tar`, on the same GitHub Release as those builds.

MP3 encoding uses LAME: https://lame.sourceforge.io/

This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group. (FFmpeg's DCT code: its notice is in `licenses/ffmpeg/ffmpeg-notices.txt`.)

These are built into them. Each has its own text in `licenses/ffmpeg`.

| Part | Version | License (SPDX) | Text |
|---|---|---|---|
| FFmpeg | 9.0.2 | GPL-2.0-or-later in this build | `LICENSE.txt`, `ffmpeg-LICENSE.md` |
| x264 | stable branch, commit `b35605ac` | GPL-2.0-or-later | `x264.txt` |
| LAME | 4.0 | LGPL-2.0-or-later | `lame.txt`, `lame-LICENSE.txt` |
| Opus | 1.6.1 | BSD-3-Clause | `opus.txt` |
| libvorbis | 1.3.7 | BSD-3-Clause | `vorbis.txt` |
| libogg | 1.3.6 | BSD-3-Clause | `ogg.txt` |
| libvpx | 1.17.0 | BSD-3-Clause | `libvpx.txt`, `libvpx-PATENTS.txt`, `libvpx-x86inc.txt` |
| dav1d | 1.5.4 | BSD-2-Clause | `dav1d.txt`, `dav1d-PATENTS.txt` |
| zlib | 1.3.2 | Zlib | `zlib.txt` |
| Code from other projects inside FFmpeg and the libraries above | | BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, MIT, ISC, Zlib, IJG, BSL-1.0 | `ffmpeg-notices.txt` |
| mingw-w64 runtime (Windows) | 11.0.1 | ZPL-2.1, with the notices in its text | `mingw-w64-runtime.txt` |
| GCC runtime, libgcc (Windows) | 13.2.0 | GPL-3.0-or-later WITH GCC-exception-3.1 | `gcc-runtime-exception.txt`, `LICENSE-GPLv3.txt` |

Some of their source files hold code from other projects, like MIPS's fixed-point code, WebRTC's iLBC decoder, musl's `sscanf` and x86inc.asm. `ffmpeg-notices.txt` has each of those notices verbatim, with the files it's in; Grape's build checks that it has every one in what it compiles. libvpx and dav1d come with patent grants, the `-PATENTS.txt` files. The GCC Runtime Library Exception lets libgcc's code be distributed under any terms, so it doesn't change the programs' license. `grape-ffmpeg-sources.tar` also holds the mingw-w64 runtime's source.

